            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.9,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.138,
            0.902,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { ~ A ~ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is very close to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , BC gets very close to 0 and so the value of sin "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { B C } } { \\mathrm { A C } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is very close to 0. Also, when "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { A }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is very close to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , AC is nearly the same as AB and so the value of cos "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { A B } } { \\mathrm { A C } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is very close to 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.258,
            0.9,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This helps us to see how we can define the values of sin A and cos A when "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { A } = 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ".",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We define : sin "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { 0 } ^ { \\circ } = \\mathbf { 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and cos "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { 0 } ^ { \\circ } = \\mathbf { 1 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.309,
            0.372,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using these, we have :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.34,
            0.798,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "tan "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 ^ { \\circ } = { \\frac { \\sin   0 ^ { \\circ } } { \\cos   0 ^ { \\circ } } }   = 0 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cot "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 ^ { \\circ } = { \\frac { 1 } { \\tan 0 ^ { \\circ } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ,   which is not defined. (Why?)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.396,
            0.899,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "sec "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 ^ { \\circ } = { \\frac { 1 } { \\cos   0 ^ { \\circ } } } = 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and cosec "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 ^ { \\circ } = \\frac { 1 } { \\sin 0 ^ { \\circ } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which is again not defined.(Why?)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.444,
            0.902,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, let us see what happens to the trigonometric ratios of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , when it is made larger and larger in   ABC till it becomes "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "90^{\\circ}.\\mathrm{As} \\angle \\mathrm{A}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " gets larger and larger, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " gets smaller and smaller. Therefore, as in the case above, the length of the side AB goes on decreasing. The point A gets closer to point B. Finally when "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { A }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is very close to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { ~ C ~ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " becomes very close to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the side AC almost coincides with side BC (see Fig. 8.18)."
            }
          ]
        },
